This directory holds the introduction pages shipped inside the CIRRUS workshop
image, copied here at session startup. The main page is the README.md in the
directory above this one, installed the same way.

BOTH ARE REBUILT FROM THE IMAGE EVERY TIME A SESSION STARTS. Anything you add or
change in here is lost at the next launch, and the files themselves are mode
0444 so that an editor refuses to save over them rather than letting you lose
an edit silently.

That is deliberate: it is what makes corrections to the material arrive without
anyone re-copying anything.

Your own work goes in the parent directory -- ~/cirrus-workshop -- which is on
your GLADE home and persists.

The entrypoint checks for this file before replacing the directory. A directory
of the same name WITHOUT this file is assumed to be yours and is left alone; the
main page is guarded the same way, by a marker comment on its first line.
